# API Testing

- This repo follows a strict no-mocking policy for backend tests.
- Integration tests target a live running server and should not invent in-process shortcuts unless the existing suite already does.
- Create a session first with `POST /api/sessions`, extract the JWT, then call protected APIs with `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
- Include `Origin: https://test.example.com` in integration requests that mirror production checks.
- Prefer explicit `PORT` when running tests because the repo still contains mixed fallbacks (`3000` and `3050`).
- Use unique identifiers with timestamps and clean up test data when the flow creates persistent records.
- Use `config/0012589021.json` as the face sample when a biometric flow needs test input.
- Test both success and failure paths, especially validation and unauthorized cases.

## Examples

```js
// Prefer
.set("Origin", "https://test.example.com")
.set("Authorization", `Bearer ${token}`)
